# Task: Make the system journal persistent

The system journal is currently stored only in volatile memory and is lost on every reboot.

Configure systemd-journald to store its journal persistently on disk. Create the drop-in configuration file `{{dropin_file}}` that sets the journal storage mode to persistent, and make sure the persistent journal directory `/var/log/journal` exists and is in use by journald.

The configuration must persist across reboots.
